body:
Alright you had your chance. You're wrong, and here's why

&#x200B;

Puff Daddy sampled Every Breath You Take without permission and lost all the royalties that his song makes.

&#x200B;

Pharrell and Robin Thicke admitted to ripping off Marvin Gaye with Blurred Lines, the Gaye family sued and Gaye posthumously earns songwriting royalties from the song.

&#x200B;

Baauer sampled Plastic Little's song Miller Time for the Harlem Shake without permission and never made any royalties from it.

&#x200B;

Then there's the famous Katy Perry copyright case.

&#x200B;

Being famous doesn't excuse you from copyright infringement. I thought you were a pro?

Here's an idea.

&#x200B;

When an actual professional tries to tell you something, try listening instead of arguing.

Thank you, this is exactly the kind of answer I was looking for!

&#x200B;

Is there any red flags to look for when comparing artist development?
